===Etymology 1===
{{back-form|en|morpheme}}, from {{der|en|grc|μορφή|t=form, shape}}. Compare {{cog|de|Morph}}, from {{m|de|Morphem}}.  Attested since the 1940s.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|grammar}} {{lb|en|grammar|linguistics}} A [[recurrent]] [[distinctive]] [[sound]] or [[sequence]] of sounds representing an [[indivisible]] [[morphological]] form; especially as representing a [[morpheme]].
# {{lb|en|linguistics}} An [[allomorph]]: one of a set of realizations that a morpheme can have in different contexts.

