===Etymology 3===
{{clipping|en|metamorphose}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial|ambitransitive|computer graphics}} To [[change]] [[shape]], from one [[form]] to another, through [[computer]] [[animation]].
# {{lb|en|science fiction|fantasy}} To [[shapeshift]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=w:Peter David|title=The Siege|passage=Meta leapt forward. In midair his lower half '''morphed''', and suddenly he was one-half humanoid, one-half coiled spring.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=30 January 2015|author=Dan Shive|title=El Goonish Shive - EGS:NP|section=Comic for Friday, Jan 30, 2015|sectionurl=https://www.egscomics.com/egsnp/2015-01-30|format=webcomic|text="Would it reflect badly on women if I '''morphed''' my bust size up a bit for it?  Sorta like wearing a padded bra?"}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} To undergo [[dramatic]] [[change]] in a [[seamless]] and [[barely]] [[noticeable]] fashion.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=June 18 2013|author=w:Simon Romero|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/19/world/americas/brazilian-leaders-brace-for-more-protests.html|title=Protests Widen as Brazilians Chide Leaders|journal=w:New York Times|accessdate=21 June 2013|passage=By the time politicians in several cities backed down on Tuesday and announced that they would cut or consider reducing fares, the demonstrations had already '''morphed''' into a more sweeping social protest, with marchers waving banners carrying slogans like “The people have awakened.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Astra Taylor|title=The People's Platform: Taking Back Power and Culture in the Digital Age|year=2014|publisher=Henry Holt and Company|isbn=978-0-8050-9545-6|chapter=2|quotee=w:Richard Florida|passage=“Highbrow and lowbrow, alternative and mainstream, work and play, CEO and hipster are all '''morphing''' together today,” [Richard] Florida enthuses.}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[computer]]-[[generated]] [[gradual]] change from one [[image]] to another.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Vivian Carol Sobchack|title=Meta Morphing|page=123
|passage=But what is this metasubstance that blinks at us from the apex of the '''morph''', and that in ''Terminator 2'' is hyperbolized in the quicksilver substratum of the T-1000?}}

